      "narrative": "Pinal County home prices are trending downward: the median sale price was $371,514, down 1.1% year over year and 2.2% from the prior month.[4] Inventory stood at 2,657 homes for sale, with 3.5 months of supply and 77 days on market, giving buyers more choice and reducing seller leverage.[4] Buyer activity appears selective, with 34.48% of listings pending, the highest pending ratio among the compared Arizona areas, while homes sold for a median 98.8% of list price in one local ARMLS market.[1][3] Construction is adding potential supply, as one report cited more than 14,000 residential units approved in the prior year, though that figure was not independently corroborated in the available sources.[6]",
