      "narrative": "Pima County’s median asking price was $372,500 in September 2026, down 3.25% year over year, while the median sale price was reported at $369,174, up 2.5% year over year.[1][2] Inventory stood at 3,851 homes for sale, with a 58-day median time on market in the Realtor.com-based county figures; another market report recorded 69 days and 3.8 months of supply.[1][2] The 0.3406 pending ratio and longer marketing times indicate more negotiating room for buyers than in a tightly constrained seller’s market.[1] A county economic plan cited more than $3.6 billion in prior investment, including 180 direct jobs and about 3,000 construction jobs, supporting construction and employment as notable local drivers.[7]",
